ough are you risking your life  when you go to these trampoline parks  yes unknowingly for families like Nick's  the message is simple never birthday  parties no never never never never you  believe they're that dangerous I don't  know how to believe any other way right  my husband was an elite-level  gymnast in response to the deaths and  injuries the International Association  of trampoline parks told us there are  parks that do not adhere to technical  industry standards and do not operate  with safety at the forefront of their  agendas the group will launch an  initiative this summer to require  third-party inspections to ensure the  safest experience possible the problem  with that is out of the 800 trampoline  parks in the US only 25% of them are  members how can you tell if the one in  your community is meeting standards you  would have to go and find out if they  are you know following these standards  but the problem is when you go into  these trampoline parks you see the signs  you're risking injury you're risking  death everything supervision because nor  I mean we had a trampoline in my  backyard and there had to be an adult  there watching to make sure at that park  that we went to outside Chicago there  was a guard over here a lot of kids  jumping over here you know they need  more supervision that's the big I know  it's fun but it's you know I'm a little  scared looking at your piece what  about people that like Anthony said have  trampolines at home that's so the  American Academy of pediatricians they  warned they advise against backyard  trampolines but the expert in our piece  said in the big picture he thinks those  are safer under adult supervision I also  talked to a trauma surgeon out in Utah  who said he can fix those broken wrists  from a backyard trampoline but the  injuries the open wound fractures coming  in from trampoline parks it's really  hard war zone injuries very important  story thank you very much meg

